    "checkedOn": "2026-10-25",
    "reason": "UCR offers useful comparative private law, public and international law, transnational business law, accounting and economics. The proposed programme nevertheless gives most of its legal weight to broad public/criminal/EU/international fields, with only one comparative private-law course. It does not sustain the family, succession, property-transfer, transaction-tax and notarial professional-rule sequence that defines Notarial Law. Adding finance, entrepreneurship or social methods does not repair that missing disciplinary substance. No complete defensible UCR programme is established; the finding does not depend on professional licensing or identical national-law coverage alone.",
